From 1b5f3c4ddd741e4e19b10e960d20cadeb97a8269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 10:11:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 777/913] dts: stm32: Use a generic name for the PMIC node

The ePAPR standard says that: "the name of a node should be somewhat
generic, reflecting the function of the device and not its precise
programming model."

So, change the stpmic binding document to use a generic name
with pattern: "^pmic@[0-9]$" and update the associated device tree,
using a alias with the real model of PMIC: STPMIC1 or STPMIC25.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a7a1ff3178f965209347aa1d57d443a0cc070d80 dts: stm32: Use a generic name for the PMIC node]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I7013cddf47ce7464e40fd56622521f1b1aebbaad
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/579264
